## Canonical command surface
Add `newrelic` under the existing `service` namespace in `shared/command-contract.json`. Every action supports `--json`; every remote action except `profiles` supports `--profile PROFILE`.

Read actions:
- `profiles`: list configured profiles with account/endpoint metadata and `has_api_key`; never expose key values.
- `auth-test`: validate the selected API key and account through NerdGraph.
- `whoami`: return the authenticated NerdGraph user.
- `applications [--query TEXT] [--limit COUNT]`: paginated REST v2 APM application inventory.
- `application APP_ID`: one REST v2 application.
- `hosts APP_ID [--query TEXT] [--limit COUNT]`: paginated application hosts.
- `deployments APP_ID [--since DATE] [--until DATE] [--limit COUNT]`: paginated application deployments.
- `violations [--policy ID] [--entity TEXT] [--priority critical|warning|all] [--limit COUNT]`: legacy open-violation view retained for current workflows.
- `issues [--state activated|closed|all] [--priority critical|warning|all] [--entity TEXT] [--since DATE] [--until DATE] [--limit COUNT]`: NerdGraph AI issues.
- `incidents [--issue ID] [--condition ID] [--entity TEXT] [--since DATE] [--until DATE] [--limit COUNT]`: `NrAiIncident` investigation rows.
- `errors APP_ID [--hours HOURS] [--limit COUNT]`: existing `TransactionError` summary/facets/timeline behavior; default one hour.
- `nrql [QUERY] [--file PATH]`: arbitrary NRQL; require exactly one source. Use a GraphQL variable rather than interpolating NRQL into GraphQL text.
- `entities [--query TEXT] [--domain DOMAIN] [--type TYPE] [--limit COUNT]`: cursor-paginated entity search.
- `dashboards [--query TEXT] [--owner EMAIL] [--limit COUNT]`: dashboard inventory.
- `dashboard DASHBOARD_GUID`: dashboard metadata, pages, widgets, visualization, layout, linked entities, and raw configuration.
- `dashboard-export DASHBOARD_GUID [--format json|terraform] [--output PATH] [--apply] [--force]`: default JSON to stdout; Terraform generates `dashboard.tf`, `provider.tf`, `variables.tf`, and placeholder-only `terraform.tfvars.example`. Supplying `--output` plans a workspace-local write; `--apply` performs atomic writes; `--force` is required for replacement.
- `alert-policies [--query TEXT] [--limit COUNT]`: alert policy inventory.
- `alert-policy POLICY_ID`: policy metadata and linked conditions.
- `alert-conditions [--policy ID] [--entity GUID] [--type TYPE] [--query TEXT] [--limit COUNT]`: REST/NerdGraph condition inventory, including NRQL, APM, external-service, and synthetics condition types.
- `alert-condition CONDITION_ID`: one condition with signal, terms, NRQL, policy, entity, enabled state, and timestamps.

Apply-gated NerdGraph actions:
- `alert-condition-create POLICY_ID DEFINITION_FILE --confirm-policy POLICY_ID [--apply]`: static NRQL conditions only.
- `alert-condition-update CONDITION_ID DEFINITION_FILE --confirm-name CURRENT_NAME [--apply]`: static NRQL conditions only; re-read and verify after apply.
- `dashboard-create DEFINITION_FILE --confirm-account ACCOUNT_ID [--apply]`.
- `dashboard-page-create DASHBOARD_GUID DEFINITION_FILE --confirm-dashboard DASHBOARD_GUID [--apply]`.
- `dashboard-page-update PAGE_GUID DEFINITION_FILE --confirm-name CURRENT_NAME [--apply]`.
- `dashboard-widget-create DASHBOARD_GUID PAGE_GUID DEFINITION_FILE --confirm-dashboard DASHBOARD_GUID [--apply]`.
- `dashboard-widget-update WIDGET_GUID DEFINITION_FILE --confirm-name CURRENT_TITLE [--apply]`.

All mutation actions return a redacted planned change when `--apply` is absent and make zero mutation calls. Applied actions require the matching confirmation, accept only configured success/GraphQL result shapes, and re-read the created or updated resource before reporting success. No delete operation is present.

## Credentials and profile compatibility
Create `NewRelicCredentials.groovy` using `PropertiesSupport` without changing Jenkins behavior.

Profile selection precedence:
1. `--profile`.
2. `NEW_RELIC_PROFILE`, then `NEWRELIC_PROFILE`.
3. `config.adapters.newrelic.default_profile`.
4. shared rule `default_profile`.

Per-field precedence:
1. `NEW_RELIC_API_KEY`/`NEWRELIC_API_KEY`, `NEW_RELIC_ACCOUNT_ID`/`NEWRELIC_ACCOUNT_ID`, `NEW_RELIC_REST_URL`, and `NEW_RELIC_GRAPHQL_URL`.
2. Canonical Jenkins-style profile keys: `PROFILE.api_key`, `PROFILE.account_id`, `PROFILE.rest_url`, `PROFILE.graphql_url`.
3. Current compatibility keys: `PROFILE.newrelic.api_key`, `PROFILE.newrelic.account_id`, plus global `newrelic.url`.
4. Legacy unprefixed `newrelic.api_key` and `newrelic.account_id` for the default profile.
5. Non-secret workspace/shared defaults.

The existing `cue.newrelic.*` and `konto.newrelic.*` keys therefore work unchanged. Public profile output contains profile id, account id, endpoints, source labels, and booleans only. License keys are not part of this operator.

## Shared rules and schemas
Create `shared/newrelic-operator-rules.json` with:
- EU REST v2 and NerdGraph defaults.
- REST path templates for applications, hosts, deployments, violations, policies, and conditions.
- NerdGraph operation names used by audited sessions: user, entity search, entity/dashboard detail, AI issues, NRQL, `alertsNrqlConditionStaticCreate`, `alertsNrqlConditionStaticUpdate`, `dashboardCreate`, `dashboardCreatePage`, `dashboardUpdatePage`, `dashboardCreateWidget`, and `dashboardUpdateWidget`.
- Timeouts: read 15 seconds, mutation 30 seconds.
- Response bounds: 4 MiB success, 8 KiB error.
- REST pagination: maximum 100 pages; entity cursor maximum 100 pages.
- Default/max limits for applications, hosts, deployments, violations, issues, incidents, NRQL rows, entities, dashboards, policies, and conditions.
- Definition-file maximum 1 MiB.
- Allowed GraphQL mutation names and accepted HTTP codes.

Create:
- `schemas/newrelic-operator-config.schema.json` for non-secret defaults and limits.
- `schemas/newrelic-operator-report.schema.json` covering all 27 operations.
- `schemas/newrelic-alert-condition-definition.schema.json` for static NRQL condition name, enabled state, NRQL query, signal settings, and terms.
- `schemas/newrelic-dashboard-definition.schema.json` with reusable dashboard/page/widget definitions matching observed NerdGraph input shapes.

Definition and NRQL files must be canonical workspace-contained regular files, not symlinks, valid UTF-8, NUL-free, and within the configured size bound. Reports include path, size, and SHA-256 only, not complete definition contents.

## Transport and adapter
Create `NewRelicGraphqlClient.groovy`:
- `query` permits semantically read-only GraphQL POST operations.
- `mutate` rejects calls unless `apply=true` and rejects mutation names not allowlisted by rules.
- Both methods use bounded `JsonWriteHttp`, validate HTTP and GraphQL error shapes, and never include headers or API keys in exceptions.

Create `NewRelicAdapter.groovy`:
- Use `ReadOnlyHttp` for REST GET and `NewRelicGraphqlClient` for NerdGraph.
- Implement all 20 read actions and seven mutation actions.
- Paginate REST pages and NerdGraph cursors with deterministic de-duplication and truncation reporting.
- Parse date-only values as full UTC days and ISO 8601 values as exact instants; report effective dates rather than null defaults.
- Escape all REST query values and all constructed NRQL string literals.
- Preserve arbitrary NRQL exactly as UTF-8 input and pass it as a GraphQL variable.
- Normalize legacy REST, AI issue, incident, NRQL, entity, dashboard, alert policy, and condition responses into deterministic maps.
- Keep GraphQL query POSTs distinct from mutations so dry-run gating never blocks reads and no coding path can bypass mutation gating.
- Compare post-apply resources with the planned normalized target before setting `applied=true`.

